  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material making a sexualized joke about hands",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text_chunk 'it might look fucked up, but her handjobs are fucking unbelievable' because the meme uses this text to create a degrading, objectifying joke. The text directly addresses the viewer's perception of the visual material (the X-ray hands) and implies the user is the one making the judgment or experiencing the humor, even though the text does not contain explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me'. The projection is indirect but strong, as the user is expected to identify with the perspective of the joke-teller or the target of the joke, which is the person whose hands are shown. The user is thus projected onto the textual material as the source of the judgment or the recipient of the degrading humor.",
